{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1093458-house-boons-and-flaws-better-now-or-worse","id":1093458,"title":"House Boons and Flaws. Better now or worse?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-16T17:02:50-07:00","id":1093458,"title":"House Boons and Flaws. Better now or worse?","content":"I want to hear what folks think of the new House Boons an Flaws. <br /> Some stay very much the same, but others... wow. I'm looking at you Gwydion and Daireann when it comes to the biggest, or most jarring changes to them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1697-lostkith","name":"Lostkith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1697_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-16T17:32:06-07:00","id":1093463,"title":"","content":"Overall a huge improvement, especially for ones that had huge playability issues before, at least as far as flaws. I'm not a fan of a few of them (the Dougal flaw.. it's not really bad, I just don't really like it thematically), but a bunch of the changes were very needed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","user":"MarkK","date":". 05-16-2017, 08:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-16T17:43:54-07:00","id":1093468,"title":"","content":"I think the Leanhaun flaw is sublime, dougal is interesting but i want to see it in play? I am interested in the implications for the monarchs of Dougal (especially Lenore for some reason). <br /> <br /> Liam got a nice facelift. Im not sure how i feel about Danan tbh (but that also came about so late in second ed im not sure how i felt about it then either). Beaumayn is wonderful","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5533-cameraobscura83","name":"CameraObscura83","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5533_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-16T18:25:45-07:00","id":1093482,"title":"","content":"Gwydion is still underwhelming and so is Eiluned in comparison to the fantastic benefits and magic other Houses get (-1 difficulties, curing Nightmare, +stat, etc). Eiluned needed an adjustment, considering that an auto success on Cantrips was a bit too much, but I would have let them choose one additional Realm Affinity to represent their specialty in magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13420-gl1tterboots","name":"gl1tterboots","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-16T19:42:30-07:00","id":1093504,"title":"","content":"I do kind of like that Gwydion doesn't frenzy anymore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-16T19:45:32-07:00","id":1093505,"title":"","content":"Aesin-still a bit of a mess but at least the flaw isn't as bad but with all the talk about connection to nature you'd think they'd be the ones most likely to learn primal, which basically is the same as their house boon but you know better.<br /> <br /> Ailil-still house Supervillain and proud! No changes but I always thought they had a good set.<br /> <br /> Balor-lost one of its 3 flaws(They can be seelie now), but kept both the wp cap and the physical deformity. The ability to touch and use cold iron seems of questionable utility vs say Silver in Werewolf as their only real advantage its kind of only a Nuclear option.<br /> <br /> Beaumayn-have a decently powerful and thematic boon and a continued extremely random flaw. No real change.<br /> <br /> Danaan-New Boons are pretty powerful for an all Dreaming game with the Flaw pretty useless for said all Dreaming Game. I don't think the need a flaw that makes them even mroe likely to go &quot;fuck the autumn world.&quot;<br /> <br /> Dairean-Um.. why is this an Unseelie House. No really their boon is dedicated to Honor, their flaw is also dedicated to the concept of hospitality. The writeup talks about all their potential power as herbalist and the sinster poison possibilities but the only real way they can be a dick in an entirely seelie way of &quot;never forget a debt&quot;<br /> <br /> Dougal-Now better than Nockers! Flaw roughly the same.<br /> <br /> Eiluned-notably unchanged overpowered boon with &quot;Hey get involved wtih plot&quot; as your flaw...<br /> <br /> Fiona-same boon, new flaw that makes them all crazy risky. Not so sure on this.<br /> <br /> Gwydion-same boon, I personally would have made it house Eiluned AND Ailil who are immune because Ailil get all sorts of bonuses to lying along with being the Brother House to the Eiluned. I like the flaw change from would be berserkers to revenge prone bastards who care only about their honor.<br /> <br /> Leanhaun-they are now playable. They are still life drainers to keep their youth but now its much more manageable on Ravaging vs needing to destroy someone by their greatest work every month. Similar boon.<br /> <br /> Liam-I am not sure what laying on hands to reduce Banality in a mortal does, but the nightmare stuff or Kithain is pretty useful compared to the old stuff. Their Flaw is pretty much a nonissue (can't ravage) they should proabably also have some sort of flaw tied to their status as known Oathbreakers.<br /> <br /> Scathach-still has a pretty good boon for what they were with the flaw being abit confusing Autumn SIdhe and non SIdhe members of the house are +2 difficulty when interacting with Nobles and Royalist commoners which means they have a worse reputation than.. active Oathbreakers, a House that prides itself on its Formorian Blood(oh and get to carry around cold iron!). Honestly I'd give them all the berserker flaw that the arcadians get and leave it at that. Perhaps keep with the whole &quot;they can't have Sovereign&quot;<br /> <br /> Varich-Still have their master puppeteer tricks but now have a playable flaw, honestly being unable to swear love and having difficulty with Empathy rolls might be too weak but the other end was pretty insane.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-16T21:39:55-07:00","id":1093530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1093458-house-boons-and-flaws-better-now-or-worse?p=1093505#post1093505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eiluned-notably unchanged overpowered boon with &quot;Hey get involved wtih plot&quot; as your flaw...</div> </div> </div> </div>Their boon is not at all the same and it is definitely not overpowered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13420-gl1tterboots","name":"gl1tterboots","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-16T21:59:10-07:00","id":1093535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gl1tterboots</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1093458-house-boons-and-flaws-better-now-or-worse?p=1093530#post1093530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Their boon is not at all the same and it is definitely not overpowered.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> ...for some I completely misread it. Yeah its changed and not broken.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}